he number of new strings allocated, thats what. The why probably\r\nwas that you have a large set of tests and found that this speeds them up.\r\n-->\r\n\r\nThis fixes 2 out of 3 problems that I've encountered with CMake + Ninja:\r\n\r\n1. Problem described in #1379 issue regarding \r\n```\r\n-    <TestCase name=\"# A test name that starts with a #\" filename=\"projects/<exe-name>/UsageTests/Misc.tests.cpp\" >\r\n+    <TestCase name=\"# A test name that starts with a #\" filename=\"../projects/<exe-name>/UsageTests/Misc.tests.cpp\" >\r\n```\r\n2. For Windows environment when there was relative path available replacement of  \"\\\\\" to \"/\" wasn't triggered.\r\n\r\n\r\n-------------------\r\nOn my linux environment I've noticed also a problem with escape sequence for compact.sw\r\n```\r\n- ToStringGeneral.tests.cpp:<line number>: passed: tab == '\\t' for: '\\t' == '\\t'\r\n+ ToStringGeneral.tests.cpp:<line number>: passed: tab == '/t' for: '/t' == '/t'\r\n```\r\n\r\n## GitHub Issues\r\n#1200\r\n#1379\r\n\r\n<!-- \r\nIf this PR was motivated by some existing issues, reference them here.\r\n\r\nIf it is a simple bug-fix, please also add a line like 'Closes #123'\r\nto your commit message, so that it is automatically closed.\r\nIf it is not, don't, as it might take several iterations for a feature\r\nto be done properly. If in doubt, leave it open and reference it in the\r\nPR itself, so that maintainers can decide.\r\n-->\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catchorg/Catch2/issues/1414/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catchorg/Catch2/issues/1414/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":1914450948,"node_id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTkxNDQ1MDk0OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catchorg/Catch2/issues/events/1914450948","actor":{"login":"horenmar","id":9026413,"node_id":"MDQ6VX